# Intel AX210 (8086:2725) does not survive s2idle on Framework 13 AMD.
#
# During suspend the platform drops the card's upstream PCIe port to D3cold and
# never restores power. On resume the card reads back as HW_REV=0xFFFFFFFF and
# iwlwifi's wiphy_resume spins for ~253 seconds before failing with -110, so the
# whole machine sits unresponsive for four minutes -- keyboard, touchpad and USB
# all dead, because nothing else in the kernel is making progress either. The
# card then stays dead until a COLD boot; a warm reboot does not re-power it,
# and a function-level reset is rejected because the device is already in
# D3cold and cannot be brought to D0 to be reset.
#
# Measured on this hardware, pm_test=platform with iwlwifi loaded:
#   before: PM: resume devices took 255.610 seconds  (last_failed_dev = phy0)
#   after:  PM: resume devices took   0.377 seconds  (no failure)
#
# Barring D3cold on the card is enough: the port above it can only power down
# once every child has, so refusing here keeps the whole path alive. Keyed on
# the card's PCI ID rather than a bus address, so it is inert on machines
# without an AX210 and leaves the sibling port at 0000:00:02.1 alone.
#
# pcie_port_pm=off cures it too, but disables PCIe port power management for
# every port on the machine; this stays scoped to the one broken device.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x8086", ATTR{device}=="0x2725", ATTR{d3cold_allowed}="0"
